On October 20, 2026, SK Nexilis announced a carbon-coated copper foil intended for high-silicon anodes and dry electrode processes. SKC explained that the special carbon interface was designed to reduce delamination when silicon-containing anode materials expand and contract. The company was establishing a pilot production system and targeted commercialization in the second half of 2027. The stated plan does not establish that mass production or broad customer qualification is already complete.

